## Last text from previous session

not* a defect: test28 reported "30 of 32 entries missing" in rounds 15/16, caused by the concurrent teardown. Guarding with `[ -d round_dir ]` isn't enough — a partially-completed `rm -rf` leaves the directory present with children already gone. sess20 hit the identical artifact and I reproduced it. Fixed by excluding any round teardown has been asked to remove. I verified the red before believing it, which is why it didn't end up in the ledger as a phantom defect.

**The `create_baseline_trackers` fix is in but unvalidated, and I've recorded it that way.** The finding behind it is real — `cached_gen=0, grant_gen=2019` proves a self-created directory keeps its staleness baselines at the "never set" sentinel forever, so detectors gated on `cached_grant_gen != 0` are permanently inert for it. But the A/B was counter-directional (P195: 0 with the fix off, 1 with it on, n=1 per arm). That's noise, not a refutation, and certainly not evidence of a fix. It stays at default-on as principled and harmless; the defect stays OPEN.

